name wordnet-cntlist
# cntlist.5: "The fields are separated by one space", and
#   "Each line in cntlist is of the form:   tag_cnt  sense_key  sense_number"
# The sense number is where the sense stands in the lemma's list, a key; the tag count is what the file says of the
# sense.
# The sense is the lexicalization [lemma, language, ILI] (recipes/BRIEF.md: "A sense key (dog%1:05:00::) is WordNet's
# pointer to a lexicalization: it is decomposed for its facts (lemma, type, lexicographer file), resolved through the
# highway's perf-cache to the lexicalization, and not recorded"; "A word in a language is the lexicalization [lemma,
# language, ILI]"), made of the sense key's own parts:
#   lemma: senseidx.5, "A sense_key is represented as: lemma%lex_sense", and "lemma is in lower case, and collocations
#     are formed by joining individual words with an underscore (_) character": the text before its %, an underscore
#     standing for the space between two words (domestic_dog%1:05:00:: is domestic dog), its case as WordNet writes it;
#   language: WordNet writes the language of its words nowhere but in its documentation, which calls them English
#     (morphy.7: "A transformation to a valid English string"); written en, ISO 639-3's Part1 of English (its table's
#     row eng: Ref_Name English, Part1 en), the code every WN-LMF wordnet of this lineage writes (the Open English
#     WordNet's Lexicon language="en"), so the count lands on the very strand that wordnet's sense of it is;
#   ILI: the concept the sense key names, resolved through the highway (index.sense's sense key to its WordNet 3.0
#     synset offset, CILI's offset to its ILI: type sense_key ili).
match cntlist

tier row by \n
names tag_cnt sense_key sense_number
tier field by space

# Canonical ISO 639-3 English hub, shared with WN-LMF lexicalizations.
thing row sense_key matching ^([^%]+)% space _ literal eng sense_key
type sense_key ili
omit sense_number
content tag_cnt
# cntlist.5: "tag_cnt is the decimal number of times the sense is tagged in the corresponding semantic concordance": a
# number the file states of the sense, an observation, said of the lexicalization (translate orders a word's senses by
# it: Laplace-Wiki Sequence/Web.md 15.6, "ordered by observed usages").
relation "number of times the sense is tagged" tag_cnt
attest row tag_cnt
